{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773084873,"nonce":"i+88D/fphOt1gzvWocjnXMjbzuQ=","title":"Future: shared graph rendering infrastructure module for Mandible + HumbleB","message":"Long-term consideration: if HumbleB gains more specialized visual representation (see HumbleB issue cf51a72), and Mandible builds out its GraphView (see #fe566dc), there may be value in extracting shared low-level graph rendering primitives into a common module (e.g. `@mll/graph-canvas` npm package) that both apps depend on.\n\nCandidates for sharing:\n- Typed node/edge wire format (`{ nodes: GraphNode[], edges: GraphEdge[] }`)\n- D3 or Sigma setup boilerplate and lifecycle management\n- Basic layout configuration (force parameters, DAG options)\n- Common interaction patterns (hover tooltip, selection, click-to-navigate)\n\nNot a near-term requirement. Both apps should develop their graph views independently first. This issue is a reminder to avoid architectural decisions that would make the extraction unnecessarily painful.","files":null}]}